# The Arrhenius rate law, as BioNetGen's network builds it (issue #107).
#
# BioNetGen gives a rule with Arrhenius(phi, Ea0) the rate
# exp(-(Ea0 + phi*dG)), with dG the free-energy change of the reaction the
# rule writes, and the reverse half of a reversible rule
# exp(-(Ea0 + (1-phi)*dG)), with dG its own reaction's (RateLaw.pm,
# evaluate_local).  There is no RT: energies are in units of RT.  The model
# has no parameter named RT; RuleMonkey divided every exponent by 2.478 when
# a model had none.  phi = 0.3, so a rule that takes phi where BioNetGen
# takes 1-phi, or the reverse, shows.  RuleMonkey gave every bond-breaking
# rule the reverse-half term, and every bond-making rule the forward one.
#
#   Rev_bound    `Ra(b) + Rb(a) <-> Ra(b!1).Rb(a!1)` with dG = ln(100):
#                k_on = 1e-5 per pair, k_off = 1e-3.
#   Revu_bound   `Qa(b!1).Qb(a!1) <-> Qa(b) + Qb(a)`, the same kind of rule
#                written in the unbinding direction, with dG = ln(10) for the
#                binding: unbinding takes phi, 1e-4; binding takes 1-phi,
#                1e-5 per pair.  RuleMonkey swapped the two terms.
#   Bind_uni     `Ua(b) + Ub(a) -> Ua(b!1).Ub(a!1)`, unidirectional, with
#                dG = ln(10): 1e-6 per pair.
#   Break_uni    `Va(b!1).Vb(a!1) -> Va(b) + Vb(a)`, unidirectional, breaking
#                a bond with dG = -ln(10): phi on the unbinding dG = ln(10),
#                1e-3.  RuleMonkey took (phi-1) on the binding dG instead.
#   Ctx_pair     `Sc(a) + Sa(s) <-> Sc(a!1).Sa(s!1)` with dG = ln(10), and a
#   Ctx_bare     cooperative pattern Sa.Sc.Sb worth -2*ln(10): an Sa binds a
#                scaffold that already holds an Sb (Ctx_pair) with net
#                dG = -ln(10), and a bare one (Ctx_bare) with dG = ln(10).
#   Rename_uni   Break_uni's rule, labelled `_reverse_Gone` with no rule
#                Gone (issue #109): BNG2 writes a reverse half under the name
#                `_reverse_` plus its forward rule's, but a rule written under
#                that name is a rule as written, and takes phi: 1e-3, as
#                Break_uni.  RuleMonkey gave it 1-phi, 3.98e-4.
#   Rename_other The same, labelled `_reverse_Flip` beside an unrelated rule
#                Flip: still a rule as written, 1e-3.  A reverse half has its
#                forward rule's rate constants and mirror-image operation.
#   Rev_consts   `_reverse_Kc`, the mirror image of an Arrhenius rule Kc but
#   Rev_samekind with other rate constants; `_reverse_Ko`, a second copy of the
#   Rev_sites    unbinding rule Ko; and `_reverse_Gx`, an unbinding whose
#                Arrhenius rule Gx binds other molecules.  None is a reverse
#                half, so each takes phi: Rev_samekind decays at 2e-3, Rev_sites
#                at 1e-3, and Rev_consts unbinds at 1e-3 while Kc rebinds.
#   Plus_bound   `Pc(b!1).Pd(a!1) -> Pc(b) + Pd(a)` under a cooperative
#   Plus_free    pattern written with `!+`, Pc(b!1,c!+).Pd(a!1) worth -ln(10),
#                which the load-time expansion reads exactly (issue #109): a
#                pair whose c is bound breaks at 1e-3 * 10^-0.3, 5.0e-4
#                (Plus_bound), a bare one at 1e-3 (Plus_free).
#
# The references are BioNetGen's network, integrated (ode); every species is
# 1000 or 500 copies, so the ODE is the mean of the SSA.
begin model
begin parameters
  phi    0.3
  Gr     4.605170185988092    # ln(100)
  Ea0r   10.131374409173802   # ln(1e5) - phi*Gr
  Gq     2.302585092994046    # ln(10)
  Ea0q   9.901115899874398    # ln(1e4) + phi*Gq
  Gu     2.302585092994046    # ln(10)
  Ea0u   13.12473503006606    # ln(1e6) - phi*Gu
  Gv    -2.302585092994046    # -ln(10)
  Ea0v   6.216979751083923    # ln(1e3) + phi*Gv
  Gc     2.302585092994046    # ln(10)
  Gcoop -4.605170185988092    # -2*ln(10)
  Ea0c   13.12473503006606    # ln(1e6) - phi*Gc
  kflip  1e-3
end parameters
begin molecule types
  Ra(b)
  Rb(a)
  Qa(b)
  Qb(a)
  Ua(b)
  Ub(a)
  Va(b)
  Vb(a)
  Sc(a,b)
  Sa(s)
  Sb(s)
  Wa(b)
  Wb(a)
  Wc(b)
  Wd(a)
  Za(s~0~1)
  Pc(b,c)
  Pd(a)
  Pe(a)
  Ka(b)
  Kb(a)
  Ma(b)
  Mb(a)
  Ga(b)
  Gb(a)
  Ha(b)
  Hb(a)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  Ra(b)                     1000
  Rb(a)                     1000
  Qa(b!1).Qb(a!1)           1000
  Ua(b)                     1000
  Ub(a)                     1000
  Va(b!1).Vb(a!1)           1000
  Sc(a,b!1).Sb(s!1)          500
  Sc(a,b)                    500
  Sa(s)                     1000
  Wa(b!1).Wb(a!1)           1000
  Wc(b!1).Wd(a!1)           1000
  Za(s~0)                   1000
  Pc(b!1,c!2).Pd(a!1).Pe(a!2) 500
  Pc(b!1,c).Pd(a!1)          500
  Ka(b!1).Kb(a!1)           1000
  Ma(b!1).Mb(a!1)           1000
  Ga(b)                     1000
  Gb(a)                     1000
  Ha(b!1).Hb(a!1)           1000
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  Rev_bound   Ra(b!1).Rb(a!1)
  Molecules  Revu_bound  Qa(b!1).Qb(a!1)
  Molecules  Bind_uni    Ua(b!1).Ub(a!1)
  Molecules  Break_uni   Va(b!1).Vb(a!1)
  Molecules  Ctx_pair    Sa(s!1).Sc(a!1,b!2).Sb(s!2)
  Molecules  Ctx_bare    Sa(s!1).Sc(a!1,b)
  Molecules  Rename_uni  Wa(b!1).Wb(a!1)
  Molecules  Rename_other Wc(b!1).Wd(a!1)
  Molecules  Plus_bound  Pc(b!1,c!+).Pd(a!1)
  Molecules  Plus_free   Pc(b!1,c).Pd(a!1)
  Molecules  Rev_consts  Ka(b!1).Kb(a!1)
  Molecules  Rev_samekind Ma(b!1).Mb(a!1)
  Molecules  Rev_sites   Ha(b!1).Hb(a!1)
end observables
begin energy patterns
  Ra(b!1).Rb(a!1)               Gr
  Qa(b!1).Qb(a!1)               Gq
  Ua(b!1).Ub(a!1)               Gu
  Va(b!1).Vb(a!1)               Gv
  Sc(a!1).Sa(s!1)               Gc
  Sa(s!1).Sc(a!1,b!2).Sb(s!2)   Gcoop
  Wa(b!1).Wb(a!1)               Gv
  Wc(b!1).Wd(a!1)               Gv
  Pc(b!1).Pd(a!1)               Gv
  Pc(b!1,c!+).Pd(a!1)           Gv
  Ka(b!1).Kb(a!1)               Gv
  Ma(b!1).Mb(a!1)               Gv
  Ga(b!1).Gb(a!1)               Gv
  Ha(b!1).Hb(a!1)               Gv
end energy patterns
begin reaction rules
  Rev:    Ra(b) + Rb(a) <-> Ra(b!1).Rb(a!1)      Arrhenius(phi, Ea0r)
  Revu:   Qa(b!1).Qb(a!1) <-> Qa(b) + Qb(a)      Arrhenius(phi, Ea0q)
  Bind:   Ua(b) + Ub(a) -> Ua(b!1).Ub(a!1)       Arrhenius(phi, Ea0u)
  Break:  Va(b!1).Vb(a!1) -> Va(b) + Vb(a)       Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
  Ctx:    Sc(a) + Sa(s) <-> Sc(a!1).Sa(s!1)      Arrhenius(phi, Ea0c)
  _reverse_Gone: Wa(b!1).Wb(a!1) -> Wa(b) + Wb(a)  Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
  Flip:   Za(s~0) -> Za(s~1)                     kflip
  _reverse_Flip: Wc(b!1).Wd(a!1) -> Wc(b) + Wd(a)  Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
  Plus:   Pc(b!1).Pd(a!1) -> Pc(b) + Pd(a)       Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
  Kc:     Ka(b) + Kb(a) -> Ka(b!1).Kb(a!1)       Arrhenius(phi, Ea0u)
  _reverse_Kc: Ka(b!1).Kb(a!1) -> Ka(b) + Kb(a)  Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
  Ko:     Ma(b!1).Mb(a!1) -> Ma(b) + Mb(a)       Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
  _reverse_Ko: Ma(b!1).Mb(a!1) -> Ma(b) + Mb(a)  Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
  Gx:     Ga(b) + Gb(a) -> Ga(b!1).Gb(a!1)       Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
  _reverse_Gx: Ha(b!1).Hb(a!1) -> Ha(b) + Hb(a)  Arrhenius(phi, Ea0v)
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
